  "holistic_F_N": 3,
  "holistic_F_H": -3,
  "section_notes": "Final rules impose strict incident reporting (24h/48h) and 55 °C per-model testing with customer access but no public publication; the 5% S2 threshold is only a corrective-action trigger, not a sales ban. Remote shut-off is required on new units and retrofitted within 6 years with alternative guidance, while built-in fire suppression starts at 36 months. A mandatory recall triggers at 8 incidents/100k with prompt notices, and the serious-injury clause is absent."
